# SHA-256 checksums for the model artefacts this repository's numbers depend on.
#
# Scope, stated narrowly. These digests identify the bytes present on the author's
# machine at the time this file was written or last regenerated. They let a third
# party check that a blob obtained elsewhere is the same file. They do NOT prove
# that a past result was produced by these bytes — nothing here is a retroactive
# provenance record, because no digest was taken when those results were produced.
#
# Coverage: the two .onnx graphs (committed), their two .onnx.data weight blobs
# (not committed - see LICENSE and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md), and the six PyTorch
# checkpoints under experiments/results/ that Studies III and IV trained and
# scored (also not committed). Nothing else is covered.
#
# Verify from the repository root:   shasum -a 256 -c models/CHECKSUMS.sha256
# On a plain clone every line except the two .onnx graphs reports
# 'No such file or directory'; that is expected, not a failure of this file.
#
# This file records identity, not origin: see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
# (Getting the weights) for what is and is not known about where they came from.
